   "reasoning_summary": "The formula C14H11N3 (DoU 11) with all 1H signals in the 7.4-9.6 range implies a fully aromatic system: a benzenoid ring plus a bicyclic diazine, linked by NH or a direct bond. Twelve 13C signals for 14 carbons suggest a monosubstituted phenyl group. The 157.5 ppm carbon (8), together with the 8.57 ppm singlet-like signal (2) and the downfield 9.59 ppm signal (1, likely the NH in DMSO), best matches 4-anilinoquinazoline (C4 about 157.6, H2 about 8.58, NH about 9.7). The 7.98 ppm signal (3) fits the anilino ortho protons, and the 7.4-7.5 cluster (4-7) fits the remaining ArH. Two alternatives are retained: 2-anilinoquinoxaline, a close isomer with a similar 1H pattern, and 2-(quinoxalin-2-yl)aniline. Integrals are absent, so the proton distribution among peaks is approximate."
